WEBVTT

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.450
The left engine block
has fallen away. It's hopeless!

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.830
Don't give up! There's still hope!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.380
-Are we okay?
-Oh, God...

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.230
<i>The space plane Orion crash landed</i>

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.240
<i>in the 23rd School District</i>
<i>of Academy City.</i>

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.740
<i>The Orion came in contact with debris</i>
<i>just before making re-entry,</i>

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.830
and crash landed
due to engine failure and other trouble.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:30.290
Luckily, all 88 passengers
aboard are confirmed to have survived.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.260
<i>Repeat, all 88 passengers aboard</i>

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.050
<i>are confirmed to have survived.</i>

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.460
Come on,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.080
won't you settle for a hamburger, Index?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.920
No, Toma.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.170
I was absolutely,
positively starving last night, after all.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.090
I couldn't help it.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.140
Hmm. To forget about supper...

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.930
it feels like you've forgotten
about my existence.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.020
Right, Sphinx?

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.650
Huh. Aw, jeez, all right, all right.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.610
Eat as much as you want.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.990
You mean that, Toma?

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.780
Yeah.
A Kamijo doesn't go back on his word.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.870
SPACE ELEVATOR

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.410
Say, Toma, what's a space elevator--

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.580
Hey, Toma!

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:55.250
Miss Index. If you have a perfect memory,
why are you asking?

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.960
-Huh?
-It's that over there!

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.970
That is the space elevator!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.810
Say, Toma, has that always been there?

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.230
Yes, it has! You really are lost
when it comes to science, huh?

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.730
It was there then... and then...

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:13.980
and then, too!

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.980
It's been there, plain as day!

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.110
Wow, I had no idea.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.990
They just announced it,

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.200
but they say its speed would be
impossible outside of Academy City.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:30.660
Hmm... I can tell
that its speed is incredible.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.330
-So tell me, Toma...
-What?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.790
What is a "space elevator"?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.720
Well, you see, something
that doesn't use a rocket or shuttle,

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.470
but can lift stuff directly
into space is a space elevator.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:49.850
Oh! The side of science is trying to make
even the Tower of Babel a reality, huh?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.820
Here, Index, you can see better from here.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.880
GLORIA

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.270
The Miracle of the 88?

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:42.650
Ah, now that you mention it,
that did happen, huh?

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:43.740
It was three years ago.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.160
After the Orion accident,
the space plane program was frozen,

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:53.080
and the construction of
the space elevator went into full swing.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.330
Oh, yeah?

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.290
I just mean, it's the first space elevator
in the world.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.420
The pains it took to build it here
in Academy City is several times, no,

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:07.260
dozens of times greater
than building it at the equator.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.760
And in the face of all of that,
what has finally been completed...

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.890
is Endymion there!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.440
Its form truly is that of a bridge
to heaven rising into the sky.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.070
It's so beautiful, huh?

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.360
Yeah, sure it is.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:28.240
Ah, hey, what's that
you're listening to, Miss Saten?

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:30.910
Oh...

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.250
It's Arisa.
An artist who appears on the Web

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.120
and does a lot of street concerts.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.880
She's incredibly popular right now.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.750
I downloaded her stuff and it's great.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.970
This is just a rumor, but they say
if you listen to Arisa's songs,

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.590
good things will happen to you.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.390
Uh, listen...

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.230
Here, please, just listen for yourself.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.140
Oh, mm-hmm...

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.440
Huh?

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.190
This song...

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.610
Ah, this is her, right?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.120
Yeah, this is her, all right.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:20.920
Huh? Misaka, don't tell me
you happen to know Arisa!

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.550
Oh, uh, well...

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.470
Sissy...!

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.110
K-Kuroko...

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.610
What are you doing in here, Sissy?!

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:49.860
M-Miss Shirai, you're supposed
to be in the hospital still.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.540
It is because of things like this
that I cannot stay in the hospital!

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.540
I was going to surprise you
by leaving early,

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.790
but imagine, me being the one
taken by surprise instead!

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:07.760
If this is how it must be,
then I will also zoom...

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.720
in right next to Sissy!

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:15.260
Ah... Shirai... calm down!

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.140
Please, calm down!

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.020
Shirai!

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.600
Oh, Sissy!

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.610
Dah! Stay back!

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.120
Thank you very much.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.210
GLORIA
ALSO AVAILABLE FOR DOWNLOAD!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.260
Thank you. I'm Arisa Meigo.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.310
Ee-yow-w-w...

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.650
I-I'm sorry.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.280
Toma...

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.500
Man, that really was amazing.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.250
It was touching! Right, Toma?

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.250
Huh?

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.840
I don't listen to a lot of music,

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:38.050
but even so,
I could tell it was incredible.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.760
Mm-hmm! Mm-hmm!

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:44.230
Look. I downloaded
all of your songs onto here.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:48.650
Thank you. I'm so glad you like them.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.570
Mm-hmm. I'm kind of picky
when it comes to music.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:56.030
But Arisa, your stuff is the real deal.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.870
You're not even casting any spells,

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.490
but your music can still charm everyone.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.040
Spells?

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:10.000
O-Oh, you know...
Like a scene that is clearly portrayed...

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:13.510
For a moment, it seemed like
telepathy or something.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:14.670
But apparently, not, huh?

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.640
No, I don't think so. I'm a Level 0.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.430
Oh, you don't say.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:28.020
Mm-hmm. I was troubled by it before,

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.020
but now, I'm kind of grateful, I think.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:32.610
Hmm? Grateful?

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:38.740
I mean, if I had an ability,
I'm sure I would have turned to it.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.990
I don't think I would have
sung in the first place.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.540
-Oh?
-Is that right?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.040
Mm-hmm.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.960
I was never any good
at my studies, either.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:55.880
The only thing I could do was sing songs.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:00.510
So I decided I would do
whatever it took to sing!

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:07.640
I hope that someday,
I'll be able to sing in a large place,

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:09.310
in front of a lot of people.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.070
I guess that's what my dream is now.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:18.070
T-Toma! She's shining so brightly,
I'm being blinded!

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.740
This is much too blinding!

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:32.340
Um, would you mind?

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:35.630
Yes?

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.550
Yes, that's right.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.010
Yes.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.260
Eh? You mean it?!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.100
Th-Thank you very much!

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.060
Y-Yes! All right!

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:56.440
My audition...

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:02.740
I passed... my audition.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.200
I'm going to get my debut!

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.620
-Hooray!
-That means, you'll be a pro!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.250
Will you be on TV?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.250
Huh? TV?

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.300
Then, you'll be just like Kanamin?
That's amazing!

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:20.300
Kanamin?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.430
We have to celebrate!

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.430
Oh, mm-hmm.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:27.970
I know! We're going to have
a fancy meal right now!

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.980
Arisa, come with us!

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.560
Huh? But...

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.400
That's okay, right, Toma?

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:55.670
Huh? Your audition is related to
that Endymion thing?

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:59.130
Mm-hmm. My song has been chosen to be used

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.050
as the theme song for their campaign.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.550
I know it! It's the elevator
that goes to space, right?

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:06.600
So then, are you going to space?

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.930
I'm still not sure about that.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:11.520
I think there's an opening ceremony.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.230
-Give me a break!
-Fried oysters and...

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:24.570
Arisa, your wish has reached God, huh?

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:25.620
Mm-hmm.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.950
You see, I seem to have good luck.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:35.210
This thing now is
really thanks to my good luck.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.000
No it isn't.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.340
Huh?

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.340
Success is something...

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:46.680
that only comes to those
unafraid to stand in the batter's box.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:50.180
And swing the bat as hard as they can,
hoping to get a hit!

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:51.930
Whoops.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:58.560
You're not convincing us at all, Toma.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:02.740
Well, my bad luck is pretty hardcore.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:06.450
But you were chosen
because of your ability.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.830
You should be proud.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:10.990
Toma...

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.620
The next one's coming!

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:33.310
Ah, it's been a long time
since I've had so much fun.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.850
Thank you very much
for hanging out with me.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:44.030
I-I'm a Level 0, too, you know.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:49.240
People trying to make
their dreams come true is inspiring.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:50.990
Oh, Toma.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.950
Yeah! When I see someone
working hard toward their future,

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:55.910
it cheers me up!

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.040
You have to try hard, too, Miss Index.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:02.460
Mm-hmm. Wait, that sounded rude.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.920
I'm already working in
the fine profession of being a Sister!

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:11.050
Are you picking a fight
with the entire English Puritan Church?!

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.350
You're blowing this out of proportion.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.390
This is a personal matter, isn't it?

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.100
You could help out with housework.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.770
Be quiet! Eating is my job!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.360
Stop acting like you're all that!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.070
You should act more like a Sister!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.110
What?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.610
That was a pretty melody.
I really like it.

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:11.030
That was in one of the songs I downloaded.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.070
Does it have any lyrics?

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:15.990
I'm still making them up.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.000
Thank you so much for today.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.830
I'll let you know
when my debut concert is.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.000
-Yeah.
-We can't wait.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:36.220
Undine, by the symbol of the chalice,

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.430
that which is distilled from all things...

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.520
W-What the...?

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:53.910
Is that...?

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.450
Watch yourself, Toma!

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.000
It's a spell that uses a water element!

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.880
Which means, they must be magicians!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.980
Keep back, both of you!

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.480
Mallybath, slow him down!

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.900
-The ground!
-Jane!

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.750
Who are you?
What do you think you're doing?!

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:54.760
Was that...

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:56.550
Spell Intercept!

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:10.020
That's...

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.450
Master...

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:19.990
Why did you act on your own?
I told you to wait for my order.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.330
Hey, Stiyl!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.580
What's the big idea here?!

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.090
Fortis 931!

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.800
Your magic name?!

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.390
Are you serious?!

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:57.450
What are you waiting for?! Seize her!

00:17:58.910 --> 00:17:59.950
Arisa!

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.670
Your right hand can't eliminate matter.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.040
Toma!

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:13.920
No!

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:17.430
Stop!!

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:22.810
What just happened?

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.360
What?!

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:26.540
Evade them!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.440
What is that?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.980
<i>We are the Civil Conflict Resolution</i>
<i>and Relief Patrol,</i>

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.530
<i>under authorization from</i>
<i>Academy City's governing board.</i>

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:04.780
<i>We are now commencing</i>
<i>a special intervention.</i>

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:03.970
Stiyl! If the disturbance gets any larger,
there's going to be trouble. Fall back!

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.890
Marie! Mallybath! Jane!

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:09.260
Right!

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:21.900
Not bad.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.170
Hey, wait!

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:38.540
Why are you after Arisa?!

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:47.050
She has the potential to start
a war between our side of magic,

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:50.140
and the side of science.

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:51.760
A war?

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.020
Hey, what do you mean by--

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:22.130
W-Who are you people?

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:26.090
We are engaged in specialized activities,

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:28.260
in order to maintain
order in Academy City.

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:30.220
That doesn't tell me anything!

00:22:30.300 --> 00:22:32.600
Are you foes of that girl or on her side?

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:37.100
The combat we just went through
is part of our commissioned duty.

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:38.560
That doesn't answer my question!

00:22:40.310 --> 00:22:43.360
I'm warning you,
do not get involved with her.

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:46.440
If you become too friendly with her,
you will die.

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:16.140
Arisa?

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:18.430
Oh, are you awake?

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:21.770
Where am I?

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:24.610
At home. This is Toma's home.

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:26.110
This isn't my home!

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:30.070
Uh, I mean, more precisely,
it's the school's dorm.

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:31.780
Dorm?

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:34.990
Was there anything familiar about them?

00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:37.580
Like who those people were?

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:42.960
Mm-hmm! It's only natural
that she wouldn't know.

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:44.420
After all, that was magi--

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:48.340
Yeah, ma-ma-major power from something

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:51.680
not entirely explainable
with just science, huh? For sure.

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:54.180
Toma, do you believe it, too?

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:56.600
Huh? Believe what?

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:00.730
That there's a mysterious...

00:24:01.350 --> 00:24:04.770
power-like thing
not understood by science.

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:08.940
Well, esper abilities can be mysterious,
as far as that goes.

00:24:12.950 --> 00:24:15.740
Yeah, um... Sorry.

00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:19.040
Arisa, do you wish there was such a power?

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:23.580
The truth of the matter is, I have it.

00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:24.670
-Huh?
-Huh?

00:24:26.670 --> 00:24:29.420
It's only when I'm singing songs,

00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:33.300
but it appears I have some kind
of unquantifiable power.

00:24:34.130 --> 00:24:38.100
Even now,
I get examined regularly at Kirigaoka,

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:42.140
but as it turns out,
they aren't sure what it is.

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:46.730
I wonder, is the fact
that people listen to my songs

00:24:47.310 --> 00:24:49.320
because of this power, maybe?

00:24:49.570 --> 00:24:50.480
No!

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.860
If it were like that, then my right hand--

00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:57.410
He's right!
Arisa, your songs are for real!

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:05.330
Thank you.

00:25:16.430 --> 00:25:20.390
You know what? I wanted to
make everyone happy with my songs.

00:25:21.140 --> 00:25:24.640
I figured that by singing,
I would become happy, myself.

00:25:26.310 --> 00:25:30.860
But if someone were to get hurt
because of them, then...

00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:35.700
Don't tell me you're thinking of
backing out after passing your audition.

00:25:36.490 --> 00:25:40.200
I mean, wanting to sing
is ultimately a selfish wish of mine.

00:25:41.080 --> 00:25:43.500
And if something like
what happened earlier comes up...

00:25:44.710 --> 00:25:47.170
and if anything happens
to those around me...

00:25:49.170 --> 00:25:50.670
So you're just going to give up?

00:25:51.130 --> 00:25:54.380
You're going to cave in
to those who come at you with force?

00:25:56.590 --> 00:25:58.510
What do you really want to do?

00:26:00.680 --> 00:26:01.510
I want to sing.

00:26:02.720 --> 00:26:05.270
After all, that's all I have.

00:26:12.730 --> 00:26:13.900
Then sing.

00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:19.200
If you have the power to do
what you want to do, then do it.

00:26:20.820 --> 00:26:24.790
So let's think of some way
to let you sing safely.

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:29.710
Mm-hmm.

00:26:30.170 --> 00:26:32.840
In that case,
you can stay here for a while.

00:26:33.130 --> 00:26:33.960
Huh?!

00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:37.130
The magicians aren't likely
to make any moves in public.

00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:40.720
Besides, Toma and I are both here.

00:26:40.890 --> 00:26:42.100
Okay? Will you do that?

00:26:42.550 --> 00:26:43.390
Magic?

00:26:43.470 --> 00:26:47.350
She means the enemy!
As long as you're here, they won't attack!

00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:50.440
You don't mind?

00:26:54.110 --> 00:26:56.030
It does seem to be the best solution.

00:26:56.690 --> 00:26:59.820
All right! What's a houseguest or two,
plus a cat?

00:27:00.490 --> 00:27:03.580
I, as a Kamijo, am glad to welcome you in!

00:27:08.790 --> 00:27:12.920
Yes. The enemy
used indeterminate abilities.

00:27:13.420 --> 00:27:14.920
<i>Abilities, huh?</i>

00:27:15.250 --> 00:27:19.470
<i>Still, these days, they can come up</i>
<i>with any number of abilities, right?</i>

00:27:19.800 --> 00:27:21.300
<i>Especially in this city.</i>

00:27:22.510 --> 00:27:26.810
I believe these enemies to
have power of a quite unusual variety.

00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:31.100
I would think your ability
to control rare earth

00:27:31.350 --> 00:27:33.560
is plenty unusual as it is,

00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:35.650
Shutaura.

00:27:36.020 --> 00:27:38.690
<i>I don't mean unusual</i>
<i>in terms of being rare.</i>

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:43.030
<i>Arisa Meigo was attacked,</i>
<i>exactly as you said.</i>

00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:45.740
<i>Just who am I dealing with?</i>

00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:48.910
Are you unable to fight unless you know?

00:27:51.540 --> 00:27:54.880
By the way,
are you sure this line is safe?

00:27:55.670 --> 00:27:57.420
<i>I'm sensing some noise.</i>

00:27:57.630 --> 00:27:58.590
Noise?

00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:01.430
Oh, yes of course.

00:28:10.770 --> 00:28:13.310
<i>How's that? Is the noise gone?</i>

00:28:14.230 --> 00:28:15.060
Yes.

00:28:15.150 --> 00:28:16.770
It is? That's good.

00:28:17.520 --> 00:28:20.440
<i>If you would escort her</i>
<i>again tomorrow, please.</i>

00:28:20.530 --> 00:28:21.360
Right.

00:28:28.080 --> 00:28:29.240
<i>Listen here, Kami!</i>

00:28:29.790 --> 00:28:31.830
The best part about getting behind an idol

00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:34.420
is discovering new talent.

00:28:34.580 --> 00:28:38.340
Especially these days, with girls
like Arisa suddenly getting hot!

00:28:38.960 --> 00:28:43.220
She becomes a major deal
in the blink of an eye!

00:28:43.720 --> 00:28:46.930
You really can't get distracted
for even a second!

00:28:47.010 --> 00:28:48.100
Is that a fact?

00:28:48.640 --> 00:28:52.850
Hmm? Kami, you seem
to be in exhausted mode today.

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:54.020
I didn't get enough sleep.

00:28:55.310 --> 00:28:58.070
I've got another houseguest
staying with me.

00:28:58.150 --> 00:29:01.280
All of my pillows and blankets
have been taken.

00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:03.450
Not enough sleep...

00:29:04.700 --> 00:29:05.660
pillows...

00:29:06.570 --> 00:29:08.200
all taken away...

00:29:08.330 --> 00:29:09.160
What's wrong?

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:13.000
Okay, everyone, take your seats!

00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:16.080
Class is starting. Hmm?

00:29:16.670 --> 00:29:20.340
Kamijo, you are not looking well at all.

00:29:20.590 --> 00:29:23.420
Skimping out on sleep will not do.

00:29:24.630 --> 00:29:26.130
Then, is it okay if I sleep?

00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:31.270
Anyone who asks that
gets to start remedial classes today.

00:29:32.470 --> 00:29:33.600
Let's get through them together.

00:29:34.430 --> 00:29:35.810
Okay, Kamijo?

00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:43.650
So you see,
Toma always treats me like a child.

00:29:46.990 --> 00:29:50.370
Couldn't that be
because you're so cute, Index?

00:29:50.530 --> 00:29:52.370
Huh? Did you say something?

00:29:55.330 --> 00:29:58.290
Listen, under the circumstances,
I have to ask.

00:29:58.670 --> 00:30:00.880
Index, your relationship with Toma...

00:30:02.170 --> 00:30:03.010
what is it?

00:30:06.050 --> 00:30:09.720
Toma makes the food for me, and I eat it.

00:30:11.310 --> 00:30:15.850
Also, whenever I get into trouble,
he always helps me out, I guess.

00:30:16.140 --> 00:30:20.980
Appearances aside, Toma is
actually pretty incredible. Mm-hmm.

00:30:24.530 --> 00:30:27.320
You sure are a strange pair.

00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:30.410
Still, you're kind of neat, too.

00:30:37.660 --> 00:30:38.500
Arisa?

00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:42.340
Arisa?

00:30:45.550 --> 00:30:46.380
What's the matter?

00:30:47.630 --> 00:30:50.300
Just a second. I thought of some lyrics.

00:30:53.510 --> 00:30:56.730
<i>Is that right?</i>
<i>So that's how you make a song, then?</i>

00:30:56.810 --> 00:30:58.140
<i>Let me see, let me see!</i>

00:30:58.230 --> 00:30:59.810
No! It's too embarrassing!

00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:03.150
Eh? No fair, Arisa!

00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:07.280
<i>I'll show you when I'm done.</i>
<i>Then we can sing it together.</i>

00:31:08.650 --> 00:31:09.780
<i>Yeah, okay!</i>

00:31:10.450 --> 00:31:12.240
Promise me, all right?

00:31:13.700 --> 00:31:14.830
I'm ho--

00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:18.710
Toma?!

00:31:18.960 --> 00:31:19.870
Toma!

00:31:25.090 --> 00:31:27.920
<i>Just my luck!!</i>

00:31:30.130 --> 00:31:30.970
Tomorrow?

00:31:31.050 --> 00:31:34.760
Mm-hmm. I'm discussing my contract
with the Orbit Portal people.

00:31:35.390 --> 00:31:39.680
For real? I have to sit through
a remedial class.

00:31:40.100 --> 00:31:43.020
I can't imagine any way
I can get there in time.

00:31:44.820 --> 00:31:46.570
Entrusting this to her instead

00:31:46.980 --> 00:31:49.240
would just make me worry more.

00:31:52.360 --> 00:31:55.330
Say, isn't there
anyone else you can turn to,

00:31:55.410 --> 00:31:57.290
who might be able to go with you?

00:32:04.960 --> 00:32:07.420
Yoo-hoo! Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:32:13.260 --> 00:32:18.560
Huh? Orbit Portal is the company that had
the Orion accident three years ago?

00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:22.560
Yes. When the space plane came down,

00:32:22.770 --> 00:32:24.770
they were about to go bankrupt.

00:32:24.940 --> 00:32:27.230
But right after that,
they were bought out,

00:32:27.320 --> 00:32:32.570
and had a miraculous recovery.
They made Endymion there a reality.

00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:37.910
And incidentally,
the company president is a girl.

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:40.790
About ten years old,
if I remember correctly.

00:32:40.950 --> 00:32:43.500
You mean, at the time, she was only seven?

00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:46.960
She is just a showpiece, is she not?

00:32:47.380 --> 00:32:50.090
A "goth-loli beauty-queen president"

00:32:50.170 --> 00:32:52.470
is so over the top, it sounds fishy.

00:32:52.670 --> 00:32:57.260
Oh, not as much as bandaged,
twin-pony-tailed wheelchair girl does.

00:32:57.850 --> 00:32:59.720
Uiharu...!

00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:05.100
So, and this is just an urban legend,

00:33:05.310 --> 00:33:08.520
but there are stories that say
she's just a promotional hologram,

00:33:08.610 --> 00:33:10.940
or a robot, or something.

00:33:11.110 --> 00:33:13.860
Ha! What a load of bunk.

00:33:14.110 --> 00:33:16.200
It may not be altogether false.

00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:20.700
Don't you think she could be
incredibly doll-like in appearance?

00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:25.290
Misaka, what's the matter?

00:33:25.460 --> 00:33:28.040
Oh, this doll just seems so--

00:33:39.050 --> 00:33:41.100
I like your songs.

00:33:41.890 --> 00:33:45.100
I haven't liked anything
so much since Jenny Lind.

00:33:46.690 --> 00:33:47.810
Good luck to you.

00:33:52.320 --> 00:33:53.190
Was that...?

00:33:58.320 --> 00:33:59.410
I'm Arisa.

00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:01.410
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:34:01.580 --> 00:34:03.540
Nice to meet you.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:05.120
Nice meeting you.

00:34:05.370 --> 00:34:06.460
Thanks for your help.

00:34:06.830 --> 00:34:09.170
Oh? Who are you?

00:34:09.330 --> 00:34:12.380
O-Oh, I-I'm Miss Arisa's manager.

00:34:14.420 --> 00:34:17.840
Hmm... you're her adorable fan club.

00:34:21.300 --> 00:34:23.560
Okay! Let's do this, please!

00:34:35.610 --> 00:34:38.740
Sorry to have you
tag along this far with us.

00:34:38.860 --> 00:34:44.240
I'm so nervous!
Still, this is starting to be fun.

00:34:44.410 --> 00:34:47.290
Come on! Hurry up and get out there!

00:34:47.460 --> 00:34:48.500
B-But...

00:34:48.620 --> 00:34:51.330
Miss Saten! This way!

00:34:56.210 --> 00:34:57.470
What's Zapper doing?

00:34:59.130 --> 00:35:02.100
Well, if she's here,
nothing to worry about.

00:35:05.970 --> 00:35:07.310
She was there that night...

00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:29.960
-What happened?
-Power outage?

00:35:30.040 --> 00:35:30.870
Oh, no!

00:35:36.050 --> 00:35:39.840
Arisa Meigo is under the protection
of the Black Crow Force!

00:36:13.790 --> 00:36:14.630
You...!

00:36:21.090 --> 00:36:23.180
<i>Crow Seven to Crow Leader...</i>

00:36:23.260 --> 00:36:24.090
What?!

00:36:24.180 --> 00:36:26.550
Multiple explosives
at the base of D Block.

00:36:27.060 --> 00:36:30.640
Evacuate immediately!
All other units, lead Arisa Meigo--

00:37:05.180 --> 00:37:06.010
An explosion?!

00:37:08.100 --> 00:37:08.930
Kuroko!

00:37:09.010 --> 00:37:09.930
Got it!

00:37:10.180 --> 00:37:11.560
Here we go!

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:18.860
I can't handle all of this!

00:37:37.880 --> 00:37:41.460
Everyone, Judgment!
Is there anyone who is injured?

00:37:44.720 --> 00:37:45.630
Are you okay?

00:37:45.930 --> 00:37:46.840
Y-Yeah.

00:37:46.930 --> 00:37:47.890
That was a close call.

00:37:47.970 --> 00:37:48.800
Thank goodness.

00:37:48.890 --> 00:37:50.560
That was so close.

00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:51.810
It really is a miracle.

00:37:51.930 --> 00:37:53.560
Yeah, it is a miracle.

00:37:53.810 --> 00:37:54.810
It's a miracle!

00:38:08.990 --> 00:38:11.280
Hey, get off of me.

00:38:11.740 --> 00:38:12.620
Hey!

00:38:25.920 --> 00:38:28.930
Arisa Meigo is safe, then? How many dead?

00:38:30.010 --> 00:38:30.930
Zero?!

00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:34.180
I see. All right.

00:38:40.440 --> 00:38:41.520
Awake, are you?

00:38:42.480 --> 00:38:44.780
-Where are we?
-Don't strain yourself.

00:38:50.320 --> 00:38:52.450
What about Arisa and the others?

00:38:53.580 --> 00:38:54.490
They're safe.

00:38:55.790 --> 00:38:58.620
Both the spectators, and Arisa Meigo.

00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:00.630
And the rest of your people?

00:39:00.920 --> 00:39:04.550
My...
The Black Crow Force are all uninjured.

00:39:06.010 --> 00:39:07.970
That truly is miraculous, huh?

00:39:10.050 --> 00:39:12.390
Do not speak that word in front of me!

00:39:14.930 --> 00:39:17.850
This chance outcome just
happened to go in that direction!

00:39:19.230 --> 00:39:21.860
There's only
a random quantum-mechanical deviation,

00:39:22.400 --> 00:39:25.980
and the warped desire of people
seeking a fortuitous outcome!

00:39:28.990 --> 00:39:30.740
People are indolent and foolish.

00:39:31.610 --> 00:39:34.530
There's no such thing
as an expedient "unseen hand."

00:39:35.450 --> 00:39:39.040
I get it. You're a hard-as-tacks leader.

00:39:39.410 --> 00:39:42.960
But have you actually
ever listened to her songs?

00:39:44.170 --> 00:39:48.130
Give them a listen.
You may actually believe in miracles.

00:39:50.220 --> 00:39:51.720
Thanks to an accident,

00:39:52.140 --> 00:39:55.140
my brain has lost the ability
to recognize music.

00:39:56.970 --> 00:40:01.140
The ability to process sound, pitch,
and rhythm was the only thing that I lost.

00:40:02.100 --> 00:40:06.110
For me, a song is nothing but
a monstrous noise, contaminating the ears.

00:40:11.200 --> 00:40:12.030
I'm sorry.

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:14.780
-Your--
-Shutaura.

00:40:15.530 --> 00:40:17.330
Shutaura Sequenzia.

00:40:17.620 --> 00:40:20.500
Shutaura, I'm...

00:40:20.710 --> 00:40:24.790
Why are you apologizing?
I'm content with who I am now.

00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:29.090
As a result, I'm able to get by
without being taken in by songs,

00:40:29.260 --> 00:40:31.220
or words such as "miracle."

00:40:33.260 --> 00:40:37.100
<i>More on the bombing of</i>
<i>the Seventh School District shopping mall.</i>

00:40:37.890 --> 00:40:41.350
<i>There was an explosion in</i>
<i>the facility under the mall.</i>

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.440
<i>The cause is still under investigation.</i>

00:40:44.060 --> 00:40:48.070
<i>A live event for the singer Arisa</i>
<i>was being held at the time,</i>

00:40:48.150 --> 00:40:49.650
<i>and there were many spectators...</i>

00:40:49.780 --> 00:40:51.030
<i>It's a miracle!</i>

00:40:51.780 --> 00:40:52.740
<i>They say it's a miracle.</i>

00:40:52.820 --> 00:40:53.740
<i>Yeah, it is.</i>

00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:56.120
<i>-A miracle?</i>
<i>-Arisa is awesome!</i>

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:07.920
Are you all right?

00:41:11.550 --> 00:41:12.470
Toma...

00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:16.800
It seems weird, huh?

00:41:17.510 --> 00:41:19.470
If it really were a miracle,

00:41:19.560 --> 00:41:23.100
then the incident wouldn't have happened
to begin with, no?

00:41:23.270 --> 00:41:24.940
Put that way, maybe so.

00:41:27.440 --> 00:41:29.270
I don't understand this.

00:41:31.030 --> 00:41:33.860
Long ago,
I was apparently in another accident.

00:41:34.450 --> 00:41:35.410
Apparently?

00:41:35.990 --> 00:41:39.160
I don't have any memories
before three years ago.

00:41:41.330 --> 00:41:44.410
Even my name was given to me
by someone at the facility.

00:41:45.370 --> 00:41:48.130
I don't have anything I can call my own.

00:41:49.130 --> 00:41:53.170
But when I'm singing songs,
at least, my heart is warmed,

00:41:53.260 --> 00:41:54.920
and something wells up inside me.

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:59.390
As long as I have my songs,
I feel like I can someday take back

00:41:59.760 --> 00:42:01.430
whatever it is that I've lost.

00:42:02.640 --> 00:42:05.100
I sort of understand what you mean.

00:42:05.600 --> 00:42:08.650
At least you have
something you believe in.

00:42:10.440 --> 00:42:12.860
Which means, I'm sure you'll be fine.

00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:19.410
<i>Coming up in two days is</i>
<i>Endymion's unveiling ceremony.</i>

00:42:20.280 --> 00:42:24.000
<i>Yes. On that day,</i>
<i>our company will do all that it can</i>

00:42:24.370 --> 00:42:28.670
<i>to show all of you</i>
<i>just what a miracle really is.</i>

00:43:25.140 --> 00:43:26.770
A miraculous singing voice.

00:43:27.230 --> 00:43:29.020
She may be unremarkable,

00:43:29.100 --> 00:43:32.310
but with more effectiveness,
it'll be a powerful copy.

00:43:32.730 --> 00:43:33.860
Don't you think so?

00:43:34.150 --> 00:43:37.070
No. I don't believe in miracles.

00:43:38.030 --> 00:43:39.780
You really aren't any fun.

00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:45.950
What has kept Orbit Portal alive,
instead of crashing with Orion,

00:43:46.160 --> 00:43:47.910
is the Miracle of the 88.

00:43:49.120 --> 00:43:52.420
In one sense, miracles are
our company's greatest merchandise.

00:43:53.130 --> 00:43:55.040
The Orion incident was no miracle--

00:43:55.130 --> 00:43:57.920
Despite all 88 people surviving?

00:43:58.550 --> 00:44:00.630
If that's not a miracle, then what is?

00:44:05.810 --> 00:44:06.720
All right,

00:44:07.010 --> 00:44:11.230
all of our preparations are now in order.

00:44:11.980 --> 00:44:13.560
It's almost time, Arisa!

00:44:14.150 --> 00:44:17.780
Mm-hmm. Thanks to
all the help you all have been.

00:44:18.480 --> 00:44:21.570
-Today is my treat. Eat up.
-Really?

00:44:22.030 --> 00:44:24.570
-Oh, waitress!
-Yes!

00:44:25.660 --> 00:44:28.040
Wow! Her, of all girls!

00:44:28.740 --> 00:44:30.250
Leave it to you, Kami.

00:44:30.710 --> 00:44:31.750
Tsuchimikado,

00:44:32.290 --> 00:44:35.380
you know the reason
why Arisa is being targeted?

00:44:35.460 --> 00:44:36.710
She is a saint.

00:44:37.340 --> 00:44:40.880
Or at least, she is viewed to have
the same power as one.

00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:42.800
Kanzaki...

00:44:43.630 --> 00:44:46.800
She's ranked ninth now.
If she were to fully come around,

00:44:46.890 --> 00:44:49.720
there's a chance her power would top mine.

00:44:49.810 --> 00:44:51.430
Arisa is a saint?!

00:44:51.600 --> 00:44:53.980
Well, that's still just a supposition.

00:44:54.150 --> 00:44:56.060
Nothing has been proven.

00:44:56.560 --> 00:44:58.820
Tsuchimikado, what is your opinion?

00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:00.570
I'm not quite sure.

00:45:01.240 --> 00:45:04.320
Defining saints has always been imprecise.

00:45:04.990 --> 00:45:07.950
Maybe if you were to
let me investigate you closely

00:45:08.120 --> 00:45:10.790
from your head down to your tippy-toes...!

00:45:11.040 --> 00:45:12.410
Y-You must be joking!

00:45:13.330 --> 00:45:17.790
Either way, Academy City wants to take
her natural gifts and abilities,

00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:20.670
analyze them anatomically,
and exploit them.

00:45:21.840 --> 00:45:24.130
Particularly that loli company president.

00:45:24.880 --> 00:45:25.970
Here.

00:45:26.510 --> 00:45:27.470
The lyrics to that song.

00:45:28.260 --> 00:45:29.760
We promised to sing together.

00:45:31.850 --> 00:45:33.520
Let's celebrate!

00:45:34.640 --> 00:45:35.480
Thanks.

00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:37.100
Cheers!

00:45:39.480 --> 00:45:41.280
Wow, the three-legged race?

00:45:41.360 --> 00:45:42.820
And with Miss Misaka!

00:45:43.440 --> 00:45:47.780
Yes. She was so insistent,
and I couldn't very well turn her down--

00:45:48.820 --> 00:45:49.660
What the...?

00:45:49.740 --> 00:45:50.910
W-What is going on?!

00:46:00.210 --> 00:46:02.340
Huh? What are you saying?

00:46:06.050 --> 00:46:07.180
Index?

00:46:08.220 --> 00:46:09.260
What's up?

00:46:09.390 --> 00:46:10.220
Huh?! Arisa?!

00:46:11.260 --> 00:46:13.930
Crow Leader to Crow Four, sitrep.

00:46:14.640 --> 00:46:16.980
<i>Target is on the expressway.</i>

00:46:18.480 --> 00:46:19.560
Don't lose them.

00:46:22.480 --> 00:46:24.360
Miracles do not exist.

00:46:26.450 --> 00:46:27.910
I won't stand for it!

00:46:30.490 --> 00:46:32.700
-Um, Master?
-Hmm?

00:46:32.790 --> 00:46:34.950
You can't smoke in the car.

00:46:35.040 --> 00:46:37.080
It stunts your growth.

00:46:37.250 --> 00:46:40.250
I don't mind. I'm plenty tall as it is.

00:46:40.750 --> 00:46:43.420
No, not you! I'm talking about me!

00:46:46.340 --> 00:46:47.380
They're coming!

00:46:52.350 --> 00:46:53.850
Marie, don't let them pass!

00:46:53.930 --> 00:46:54.770
Okay!

00:47:42.440 --> 00:47:43.480
Master!

00:47:44.320 --> 00:47:45.150
Here!

00:47:48.440 --> 00:47:50.150
Innocentius!

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:13.050
They're up ahead. Teacher, please hurry!

00:48:13.140 --> 00:48:14.850
I-I know!

00:48:44.670 --> 00:48:45.710
Stop!

00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:48.420
Why jump the gun, Stiyl?!

00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:51.840
There's still no proof that she's a saint.

00:48:53.340 --> 00:48:54.180
Kanzaki...

00:48:55.640 --> 00:48:57.760
I just got new orders.

00:48:59.060 --> 00:48:59.970
Know what that is?

00:49:00.720 --> 00:49:01.980
A space elevator?

00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:02.980
No.

00:49:03.480 --> 00:49:06.610
The Sumerian ziggurats;
the Tower of Babel...

00:49:06.860 --> 00:49:09.690
When architecture exceeds rationality,

00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:13.030
at the same time,
it also takes on magical implications.

00:49:13.700 --> 00:49:16.280
There are those who would involve a saint,

00:49:16.950 --> 00:49:20.290
and try to turn it
into a grand-scale magical instrument.

00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:22.080
<i>Just a minute.</i>

00:49:22.330 --> 00:49:25.920
<i>You mean someone in Academy City</i>
<i>is trying to use magic?!</i>

00:49:26.630 --> 00:49:27.590
<i>It's me.</i>

00:49:27.710 --> 00:49:30.250
<i>Antiskill is on the move. Withdraw.</i>

00:49:30.670 --> 00:49:31.800
Acknowledged.

00:49:43.890 --> 00:49:46.520
No... it can't be...

00:49:46.900 --> 00:49:48.400
<i>Oh, you noticed?</i>

00:49:49.520 --> 00:49:52.860
<i>Fine. Bring the girl back to me.</i>

00:49:56.990 --> 00:49:57.820
Stay back!

00:49:57.910 --> 00:50:00.280
Shutaura! Let the girl go!

00:50:00.490 --> 00:50:01.330
Shutaura!

00:50:02.490 --> 00:50:05.290
It's not your business!
Why are you interfering?!

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:09.880
This is bad!

00:50:13.960 --> 00:50:15.010
Run, Toma Kamijo!

00:50:42.530 --> 00:50:43.620
Miss Saten?

00:50:45.290 --> 00:50:47.250
Hello? What's up?

00:50:50.080 --> 00:50:51.090
Huh?! Miss Arisa?!

00:50:51.630 --> 00:50:55.460
Yes. They say that it's almost certain
that she was abducted.

00:50:58.930 --> 00:51:01.010
All right. I'm heading out.

00:51:24.290 --> 00:51:26.120
Who is this girl?

00:51:27.160 --> 00:51:28.870
Why does she have this bracelet?

00:51:30.670 --> 00:51:33.420
Sure enough,
you two are drawn to each other.

00:51:34.750 --> 00:51:38.470
On that day, there were 88 passengers
and crew aboard the Orion.

00:51:39.220 --> 00:51:42.970
And following the accident,
there were 88 confirmed survivors.

00:51:43.930 --> 00:51:45.970
Everyone said it was a miracle.

00:51:47.020 --> 00:51:49.890
But the truth is,
there was a single casualty.

00:51:50.270 --> 00:51:53.440
The Orion's pilot, Daedalus Sequenzia.

00:51:55.150 --> 00:51:57.280
Yes, your father.

00:51:58.650 --> 00:52:03.280
But by the time that fact was confirmed,
it was too late.

00:52:03.740 --> 00:52:05.580
The world was caught up by the miracle.

00:52:05.660 --> 00:52:10.250
The 89th person had been covered up,
and only the miracle remained.

00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:15.670
The girl who suddenly appeared
on the plane that carried only 88 people

00:52:15.790 --> 00:52:17.130
and worked that miracle...

00:52:18.340 --> 00:52:19.260
is this girl.

00:52:20.340 --> 00:52:22.840
You persist in calling it a miracle?

00:52:23.510 --> 00:52:28.020
Well, the truth is,
nobody should have survived the accident.

00:52:29.310 --> 00:52:30.140
You don't mean...

00:52:30.230 --> 00:52:31.890
I thought it would work better in space.

00:52:32.900 --> 00:52:35.860
However, except for your father,
everyone survived.

00:52:36.730 --> 00:52:40.280
And, it did produce
an unexpected by-product,

00:52:40.490 --> 00:52:42.700
so I guess it was a success.

00:52:42.910 --> 00:52:44.370
It was you?

00:52:47.080 --> 00:52:48.290
It was because of you?

00:53:09.600 --> 00:53:10.600
Who is she?

00:53:28.330 --> 00:53:29.990
You're that guy from before!

00:53:36.210 --> 00:53:37.630
Are you through yet?

00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:42.170
I think that's the 16th time
I've been stabbed.

00:53:43.220 --> 00:53:44.340
You're a monster!

00:53:44.930 --> 00:53:45.930
Oh, am I?

00:53:46.930 --> 00:53:48.260
I may be,

00:53:49.050 --> 00:53:53.600
but you two are something else yourselves.
I'll let you live.

00:53:54.480 --> 00:53:58.440
Watch closely as
the true miracle takes place.

00:53:58.860 --> 00:54:02.230
Whatever you're scheming,
I swear I'll bring it down!

00:54:02.730 --> 00:54:03.570
I swear it!

00:54:04.950 --> 00:54:06.070
I look forward to it.

00:54:06.740 --> 00:54:07.780
Take her away.

00:54:10.870 --> 00:54:13.450
Now then, that just leaves you.

00:54:19.840 --> 00:54:20.840
Good morning.

00:54:22.590 --> 00:54:26.090
I need a favor from you, Miss Arisa Meigo.

00:54:28.720 --> 00:54:32.760
<i>Those with ticket numbers</i>
<i>2033 through 2152,</i>

00:54:32.850 --> 00:54:34.310
<i>please embark on the No. 17 Linear Track.</i>

00:54:34.390 --> 00:54:37.560
<i>Coming up tomorrow</i>
<i>is the grand unveiling ceremony,</i>

00:54:37.900 --> 00:54:41.570
<i>and guests for the ceremony</i>
<i>are rolling into Endymion.</i>

00:54:42.320 --> 00:54:43.820
So then, it's true.

00:54:44.280 --> 00:54:46.450
Mm-hmm. Arisa never came back.

00:54:46.530 --> 00:54:48.820
I've checked around here and there, too.

00:54:49.360 --> 00:54:50.370
I see.

00:54:51.870 --> 00:54:52.950
-Listen...
-Toma...

00:54:59.420 --> 00:55:01.250
This is a serious burn.

00:55:02.090 --> 00:55:04.760
Wish to set a new admittance record here?

00:55:05.300 --> 00:55:07.670
Uh, no, it's not like--

00:55:07.840 --> 00:55:09.340
Hi, Kami!

00:55:10.180 --> 00:55:11.300
Can we have a second?

00:55:13.810 --> 00:55:16.980
Crow Seven to all units,
system infiltration successful.

00:55:20.560 --> 00:55:22.190
We're going to settle this.

00:55:22.730 --> 00:55:23.610
Settle this?

00:55:23.820 --> 00:55:27.150
Ladylee Tangleroad was
originally someone on our side,

00:55:27.400 --> 00:55:29.400
a sybil who specialized
in Greek divination.

00:55:30.200 --> 00:55:34.580
She is trying to construct a spell
with Arisa Meigo at its core.

00:55:35.160 --> 00:55:37.910
A super-colossal one, which uses Endymion.

00:55:38.710 --> 00:55:43.670
Something in a class that would wipe out
the whole northern hemisphere.

00:55:45.210 --> 00:55:48.260
Anyhow, as long as
the problem is a magical one,

00:55:48.630 --> 00:55:52.180
this falls within our territory.
You guys keep out of it.

00:55:52.260 --> 00:55:55.430
Are you sure you can handle it?
We're talking outer space.

00:55:55.560 --> 00:55:57.060
We'll deal with the core.

00:55:57.350 --> 00:56:00.520
If it comes down to it,
we'll destroy the tower.

00:56:01.060 --> 00:56:04.230
When you say you'll deal with the core,
you mean you'll kill Arisa?

00:56:05.520 --> 00:56:06.940
That is what it means.

00:56:08.440 --> 00:56:11.490
The thing about Arisa is, she has a dream.

00:56:11.990 --> 00:56:14.700
She is putting all of her effort into it.

00:56:15.620 --> 00:56:21.000
Why should she be treated like a villain
out to destroy half the world?

00:56:25.960 --> 00:56:28.380
Toma! You shouldn't be up yet!

00:56:28.460 --> 00:56:30.720
There's no time.

00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:34.800
Whether we leave it to magic or science,
Arisa will get killed!

00:56:37.600 --> 00:56:38.930
As big a fool as ever.

00:56:39.020 --> 00:56:40.930
Wait, Toma! Toma, I say!

00:56:41.180 --> 00:56:44.060
We figured you'd say that,
so we got something ready.

00:56:45.020 --> 00:56:46.480
"Stare."

00:56:46.570 --> 00:56:51.070
"Mm-hmm, I see.
It sounds like this is big trouble,"

00:56:51.610 --> 00:56:55.700
says Misaka Misaka,
intentionally speaking out loud.

00:56:55.870 --> 00:56:58.620
Ugh... pipe down!

00:56:58.870 --> 00:57:01.910
That's too loud to be
talking to yourself. Sheesh...

00:57:06.500 --> 00:57:08.800
Say, I bought some drinks. Want one?

00:57:09.920 --> 00:57:10.760
Wait...

00:57:10.840 --> 00:57:13.180
Why, that little...!

00:57:16.260 --> 00:57:19.100
<i>Except for your father, everyone survived.</i>

00:57:19.180 --> 00:57:20.770
<i>If that's not a miracle, then what is?</i>

00:57:25.480 --> 00:57:26.650
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:57:28.610 --> 00:57:29.440
Sitrep.

00:57:29.610 --> 00:57:31.280
Ladylee and the others are in space.

00:57:31.530 --> 00:57:33.150
We are at Phase Four.

00:57:33.820 --> 00:57:36.700
<i>An Antiskill squad is</i>
<i>approaching Endymion.</i>

00:57:37.120 --> 00:57:37.950
Ready to go up?

00:57:38.490 --> 00:57:39.330
Yes.

00:57:43.370 --> 00:57:44.210
Captain...

00:57:44.330 --> 00:57:47.790
I'm going to settle this.
Don't send anyone else.

00:57:49.420 --> 00:57:50.250
I'm off.

00:58:04.690 --> 00:58:09.820
<i>We are temporarily shutting down</i>
<i>the network to adjust the relay circuits.</i>

00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:12.360
<i>Please wait until service is restored.</i>

00:58:19.530 --> 00:58:20.410
A miracle...

00:58:20.530 --> 00:58:24.660
I wonder if you would
sing for me your miracle song?

00:58:28.290 --> 00:58:29.130
Toma...

00:58:33.670 --> 00:58:35.220
Have you still not decided?

00:58:39.510 --> 00:58:43.810
But I gave such a big stage
to a mere street performer.

00:58:44.520 --> 00:58:46.270
You can always refuse.

00:58:46.940 --> 00:58:51.060
In that case, all of the guests here
will end up dying.

00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:56.240
I'll sing.

00:58:57.110 --> 00:59:01.070
But it won't be for my dream,
nor will it be for your dream.

00:59:01.830 --> 00:59:05.910
My song will be for everyone
who is genuinely looking forward to it.

00:59:07.410 --> 00:59:10.210
I will sing for those people.

00:59:10.750 --> 00:59:12.420
No matter what you are thinking,

00:59:13.210 --> 00:59:15.920
a miracle song that will rise above it.

00:59:21.720 --> 00:59:22.850
What is this?

00:59:23.310 --> 00:59:24.810
A Ballistic Slider.

00:59:25.060 --> 00:59:27.730
The unfortunate new shuttle system
that lost out

00:59:27.810 --> 00:59:31.060
as Academy City's
next mainstay space transport craft.

00:59:32.150 --> 00:59:33.820
Kami, this is your ride.

00:59:34.320 --> 00:59:35.570
Huh? To where?

00:59:36.150 --> 00:59:38.200
Why, outer space, of course!

00:59:39.490 --> 00:59:42.530
What's up with the underground tunnels
and payload routes?

00:59:43.330 --> 00:59:44.990
They are all sealed off.

00:59:45.080 --> 00:59:45.910
Which means...

00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:49.790
This bridge is the only thing we can use.

01:00:10.560 --> 01:00:11.650
Charge!

01:00:37.250 --> 01:00:38.590
It's up to you, Kami.

01:00:43.720 --> 01:00:44.640
Now then,

01:00:45.140 --> 01:00:45.970
let's go.

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:49.140
-Right!
-Right!

01:01:19.210 --> 01:01:22.260
Life and death; finite and infinite...

01:01:22.800 --> 01:01:27.390
Here where everything intersects,
different laws operate than on the ground.

01:01:28.390 --> 01:01:32.890
The fanaticism and blood of the people
are an offering to the gods.

01:01:33.600 --> 01:01:37.860
Their life's breath will strike down
Endymion's eternal curse!

01:01:40.940 --> 01:01:41.940
What is that?

01:01:42.280 --> 01:01:45.450
Amazing! I've never seen
a magic array so large!

01:01:46.110 --> 01:01:49.330
It's bringing in the earth itself
as part of the spell!

01:01:49.620 --> 01:01:51.160
What happens when it's activated?

01:01:51.580 --> 01:01:54.460
I have no idea what its objective is.

01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:58.630
I think it's Goetian in nature,
but this isn't in the records.

01:02:00.500 --> 01:02:01.800
W-What's that?!

01:02:02.550 --> 01:02:04.380
<i>Hi, Kami!</i>

01:02:05.050 --> 01:02:08.220
<i>I have some unfortunate news.</i>

01:02:08.800 --> 01:02:12.600
<i>The elevator's anti-debris missiles</i>
<i>have locked onto you.</i>

01:02:13.060 --> 01:02:15.310
But we don't have any weapons!

01:02:15.730 --> 01:02:17.400
<i>Of course you do!</i>

01:02:19.770 --> 01:02:21.860
<i>Okay, you're on!</i>

01:02:22.780 --> 01:02:26.360
Tsuchimikado, I won't forget about this.

01:03:09.070 --> 01:03:12.410
The rest is up to you, Toma Kamijo.

01:04:02.790 --> 01:04:03.630
Where's backup?!

01:04:03.710 --> 01:04:05.300
It'll be a while.

01:04:13.720 --> 01:04:17.390
Sheesh! Leave me behind
without saying anything, will he?

01:04:18.020 --> 01:04:22.350
He is so off the mark
in the way he does things!

01:04:30.070 --> 01:04:31.950
Listen, Kuroko, I need a favor.

01:04:32.660 --> 01:04:33.490
Keep things safe here.

01:04:34.990 --> 01:04:35.910
Sissy, no...!

01:04:35.990 --> 01:04:37.240
You're all I have.

01:04:38.040 --> 01:04:39.080
So please...

01:04:42.040 --> 01:04:44.040
-Sissy!
-I'm counting on you!

01:04:44.130 --> 01:04:45.290
Sissy!

01:04:50.130 --> 01:04:51.220
We should go too.

01:04:51.300 --> 01:04:52.720
-Right, Master!
-Master!

01:04:58.770 --> 01:05:00.930
There's a huge commotion down there.

01:05:01.810 --> 01:05:03.730
But you won't make it in time.

01:05:03.900 --> 01:05:05.310
I wouldn't be so sure.

01:05:18.830 --> 01:05:19.950
Silly girl.

01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:21.910
So you've come.

01:05:32.340 --> 01:05:35.640
Like I said, I swear you're going to pay!

01:05:57.160 --> 01:05:58.280
Yes...

01:05:59.740 --> 01:06:02.370
I must have lived
a thousand years already.

01:06:03.830 --> 01:06:06.080
The Orion experiment may have failed,

01:06:07.250 --> 01:06:10.960
but in exchange,
an unexpected byproduct came about.

01:06:11.500 --> 01:06:12.510
Arisa.

01:06:13.840 --> 01:06:18.220
With her miraculous power,
I will be able to die.

01:06:18.550 --> 01:06:21.010
Come, let's end this together!

01:06:24.230 --> 01:06:25.480
Oh no you don't!

01:06:56.800 --> 01:06:57.760
Toma!

01:07:04.850 --> 01:07:06.520
<i>Say, what was that just now?</i>

01:07:07.060 --> 01:07:11.770
It looks like there was an explosion
near the elevator relay station.

01:07:13.020 --> 01:07:16.320
The stress balances
are starting to come undone!

01:07:16.570 --> 01:07:17.780
Huh? But that means...

01:07:18.400 --> 01:07:21.200
If this keeps up,
the elevator will collapse,

01:07:21.660 --> 01:07:23.700
and proceed to fall to earth!

01:07:37.050 --> 01:07:38.970
-What was that explosion?
-An accident?

01:07:39.050 --> 01:07:40.390
-No way.
-I'm scared!

01:07:40.800 --> 01:07:42.470
Hey, this is outer space.

01:07:43.350 --> 01:07:44.470
What's going to happen?

01:08:00.700 --> 01:08:01.530
<i>That's right...</i>

01:08:02.570 --> 01:08:03.660
<i>That other time...</i>

01:08:04.700 --> 01:08:05.540
<i>I...</i>

01:08:06.290 --> 01:08:08.000
What are the attendants doing?!

01:08:08.080 --> 01:08:09.620
Hurry and open up!

01:08:27.350 --> 01:08:28.180
A song?

01:08:50.580 --> 01:08:52.790
Um, this way, please.

01:09:05.260 --> 01:09:08.220
That's my 38th explosion...

01:09:09.350 --> 01:09:12.020
First time I've been exposed to a vacuum.

01:09:13.810 --> 01:09:15.360
It's over, for sure.

01:09:15.980 --> 01:09:17.690
I'm going to die!

01:09:25.910 --> 01:09:27.740
Endymion is going to collapse?!

01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:31.120
<i>Yeah. Apparently,</i>
<i>the situation is unavoidable now.</i>

01:09:31.500 --> 01:09:34.250
<i>We're trying everything we can, but--</i>

01:09:35.460 --> 01:09:36.420
Tsuchimikado!

01:09:37.040 --> 01:09:38.040
Toma...

01:09:40.300 --> 01:09:41.210
Let's split up.

01:09:43.090 --> 01:09:45.640
You keep the magic from activating.

01:09:46.090 --> 01:09:47.760
I'll go get Arisa.

01:09:50.060 --> 01:09:53.140
Toma, let's save Arisa no matter what.

01:09:54.270 --> 01:09:56.850
I promised her
that once her song was done,

01:09:57.360 --> 01:09:58.940
we would sing it together!

01:09:59.650 --> 01:10:00.480
All right.

01:10:04.650 --> 01:10:08.320
<i>It's no use!</i>
<i>It looks like we can't prevent a collapse!</i>

01:10:08.660 --> 01:10:09.490
Calm down!

01:10:10.160 --> 01:10:11.830
<i>Isn't there a way?</i>

01:10:11.910 --> 01:10:12.750
Let's see...

01:10:15.420 --> 01:10:17.750
There's an emergency purge system.

01:10:18.130 --> 01:10:20.670
Normally, it would be set off remotely.

01:10:21.590 --> 01:10:24.510
Right now, the system itself is frozen.

01:10:24.720 --> 01:10:26.130
It's not working?

01:10:26.760 --> 01:10:32.600
If we can manually set off all
the blast bolts in these three spots...

01:10:34.430 --> 01:10:36.730
<i>We have to try anything we can.</i>

01:10:38.060 --> 01:10:39.940
<i>I'll take one of the locations.</i>

01:10:40.520 --> 01:10:43.360
Sissy! I am heading there now, as well--

01:10:44.190 --> 01:10:45.070
Miss Shirai!

01:10:46.400 --> 01:10:48.820
I'll take another location.

01:10:49.530 --> 01:10:51.240
Then the third one is...

01:10:51.830 --> 01:10:53.200
<i>Hello!</i>

01:10:53.950 --> 01:10:58.960
<i>This is penname, "Spelled like 'Life,'</i>
<i>pronounced like 'Sister'!"</i>

01:10:59.920 --> 01:11:01.460
I've heard what's happening.

01:11:01.920 --> 01:11:05.050
There's a way for me
to deal with the third location.

01:11:05.550 --> 01:11:06.420
Who is that?

01:11:06.510 --> 01:11:07.340
I don't know.

01:11:07.800 --> 01:11:12.390
Whoever it is, if he can break in
on an encoded Antiskill line,

01:11:12.850 --> 01:11:15.480
he's not just some rubbernecker
or prankster.

01:11:16.480 --> 01:11:19.190
<i>There you have it, Stiyl.</i>
<i>It's up to you, now.</i>

01:11:19.770 --> 01:11:22.770
Hmph, what's the use? I'm at your service.

01:11:24.360 --> 01:11:25.320
Shut up...

01:11:26.440 --> 01:11:27.900
Just shut up!

01:11:29.320 --> 01:11:31.370
This noise can work a miracle?

01:11:33.030 --> 01:11:35.870
I'll stop it... I swear!

01:11:52.140 --> 01:11:52.970
Stop...

01:11:55.010 --> 01:11:56.060
Stop!!

01:12:18.700 --> 01:12:19.620
Toma!

01:12:21.370 --> 01:12:23.040
That was cutting it close.

01:12:28.260 --> 01:12:29.130
Toma!

01:12:34.300 --> 01:12:36.310
Just a little more...

01:12:37.680 --> 01:12:38.850
Right over there...

01:12:42.400 --> 01:12:45.020
I've never seen a spell as crazy as this.

01:12:45.610 --> 01:12:47.400
Are you trying to destroy Earth?

01:12:48.480 --> 01:12:52.660
Your lines refining your magical power
are more than just a bit off the rails.

01:12:53.910 --> 01:12:56.370
The List of Prohibited Books.
I've heard of you.

01:12:57.370 --> 01:13:02.080
A human library, who has memorized
103,000 volumes of magic grimoires.

01:13:03.040 --> 01:13:04.750
You should be able to understand.

01:13:05.290 --> 01:13:07.630
How it feels to be cursed by magic.

01:13:08.750 --> 01:13:12.130
I can finally make my way
out of this hell.

01:13:12.760 --> 01:13:13.590
You can't.

01:13:14.470 --> 01:13:16.100
It won't kill you.

01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:18.180
I can tell.

01:13:19.100 --> 01:13:20.560
Why, you...!

01:13:28.270 --> 01:13:30.320
If we don't hurry, it'll be too late!

01:13:42.290 --> 01:13:43.210
Don't get careless!

01:13:43.660 --> 01:13:44.830
Master!

01:13:45.040 --> 01:13:45.960
Here they come!

01:13:48.960 --> 01:13:49.960
Toma!

01:14:01.770 --> 01:14:03.850
Don't do it, Shutaura!

01:14:04.140 --> 01:14:08.110
Her existence is
what gave rise to Ladylee's plan.

01:14:09.070 --> 01:14:10.400
As well as its unseen casualty.

01:14:11.400 --> 01:14:12.360
Her songs...

01:14:13.190 --> 01:14:15.570
and her miracles mislead people!

01:14:16.320 --> 01:14:17.200
That's why I'm killing her!

01:14:21.910 --> 01:14:23.790
Why? Why are you laughing?!

01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:30.250
<i>Miss Misaka,</i>
<i>the blast bolt is after your next right.</i>

01:14:30.750 --> 01:14:31.840
Acknowledged!

01:14:37.720 --> 01:14:39.890
<i>What's the matter, Miss Misaka?</i>

01:14:40.640 --> 01:14:42.890
Are you okay, Master?

01:14:43.390 --> 01:14:46.350
Don't worry about me. It's just a scratch.

01:14:51.440 --> 01:14:54.030
Master, let us handle this.

01:14:54.320 --> 01:14:55.150
Nonsense.

01:14:56.070 --> 01:14:59.530
I will finish the task
I've been entrusted with.

01:15:00.990 --> 01:15:03.870
This is Yomikawa. I'm sorry,

01:15:04.370 --> 01:15:06.290
but I won't reach it in time.

01:15:07.420 --> 01:15:08.580
<i>"It's all right.</i>

01:15:09.960 --> 01:15:12.590
<i>Continue to detonate on the three-count,"</i>

01:15:12.840 --> 01:15:15.050
<i>requests Misaka.</i>

01:15:15.170 --> 01:15:16.010
Sissy...?

01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:29.270
Jeez...

01:15:29.900 --> 01:15:34.030
Why do I have to come out
and do something like this?

01:15:34.230 --> 01:15:36.900
"You see, if Endymion here falls down,

01:15:36.990 --> 01:15:41.570
the earth will be ruined,
and no one will have anywhere to live,"

01:15:41.910 --> 01:15:45.080
says Misaka Misaka,
stating correct, yet obvious reasoning!

01:15:46.500 --> 01:15:51.040
Ha! The earth?
Not that it's any of my business,

01:15:51.960 --> 01:15:54.800
but, this may be perfect
for my physical therapy.

01:15:55.300 --> 01:15:57.170
No time for hesitation, huh?

01:15:57.880 --> 01:15:58.880
Here goes!

01:16:00.550 --> 01:16:01.390
Three!

01:16:07.180 --> 01:16:08.520
Two!

01:16:21.030 --> 01:16:22.780
-What was that?
-Did they do it?

01:16:23.490 --> 01:16:24.530
Take cover!

01:16:30.710 --> 01:16:33.750
Don't tell me
they're trying to purge Endymion!

01:16:35.880 --> 01:16:39.470
<i>Now I can do it.</i>
<i>Unpack the layers of her spell,</i>

01:16:40.260 --> 01:16:42.090
<i>and find some way to collapse it!</i>

01:16:44.680 --> 01:16:46.430
They detonated the base?!

01:16:46.600 --> 01:16:48.350
Now you see, don't you?

01:16:49.270 --> 01:16:51.020
There's no such thing as "can't"!

01:16:56.940 --> 01:16:59.820
My father, the pilot of the Orion,

01:17:00.780 --> 01:17:03.200
was the sole casualty of that accident.

01:17:04.820 --> 01:17:10.000
Even though I
and the other passengers. all survived.

01:17:11.370 --> 01:17:15.750
That's why I deny miracles!
To carry on the will of my father,

01:17:16.750 --> 01:17:21.380
who didn't rely on miracles
and fought only with what he had!

01:17:24.180 --> 01:17:28.260
Your old man was trying to protect
you and the other passengers.

01:17:29.350 --> 01:17:32.430
Even if the chances
were less than one percent,

01:17:33.060 --> 01:17:36.060
as long as he pushed it to the limit,
something would turn out.

01:17:37.060 --> 01:17:39.780
He believed that and hung to the end!

01:17:40.650 --> 01:17:44.740
Which is precisely the reason
why you and the others lived, isn't it?

01:17:48.990 --> 01:17:50.160
A miracle happened.

01:17:51.160 --> 01:17:54.210
Your old man is the one
who worked that miracle!

01:17:54.960 --> 01:17:57.000
And for you to deny that

01:17:57.330 --> 01:18:01.460
is the same as you killing
your old man once again, isn't it?!

01:18:09.260 --> 01:18:11.520
Come on, answer, Kami!

01:18:13.350 --> 01:18:14.190
Damn...

01:18:15.480 --> 01:18:17.310
Endymion is going to fall.

01:18:21.570 --> 01:18:25.610
To hell with the Miracle of the 88!
To hell with miraculous songs!

01:18:26.030 --> 01:18:27.780
Go ahead and save us now!

01:18:28.740 --> 01:18:33.040
Try to save everyone from
Endymion falling down to the earth!

01:18:33.660 --> 01:18:34.500
Including her,

01:18:35.120 --> 01:18:35.960
and you,

01:18:36.750 --> 01:18:40.250
and everyone who accepts miracles
that violate the natural order!

01:18:50.640 --> 01:18:51.890
Stop that!

01:18:56.310 --> 01:18:58.350
Even if you follow your way
and deny miracles,

01:18:58.900 --> 01:18:59.980
it won't bring about order!

01:19:13.040 --> 01:19:16.080
Betting on even the slightest possibility,

01:19:16.500 --> 01:19:19.250
believing that you can gain something,

01:19:19.670 --> 01:19:21.880
and making even a bit of difference

01:19:21.960 --> 01:19:23.750
is what moving forward is, isn't it?!

01:19:24.130 --> 01:19:27.840
That's what your old man
was aiming for, wasn't it?

01:19:28.380 --> 01:19:31.350
And isn't that exactly what a miracle is?!

01:19:32.300 --> 01:19:35.850
I'm going to take your miserable delusion

01:19:36.060 --> 01:19:37.890
and smash it with my right hand!

01:19:56.000 --> 01:19:59.330
Hey, Shutaura...

01:20:00.790 --> 01:20:04.210
music is a really great thing.

01:20:07.050 --> 01:20:09.970
REMAINING BATTERY LIFE HAS REACHED 0

01:20:12.850 --> 01:20:14.850
Damn...

01:20:17.520 --> 01:20:21.150
It's not... over yet.

01:20:54.140 --> 01:20:56.600
-Are we okay?
-Oh, God...

01:21:01.600 --> 01:21:04.770
The left engine block
has fallen away. It's hopeless!

01:21:05.860 --> 01:21:07.860
Don't give up! There's still hope!

01:21:11.740 --> 01:21:12.570
What is it?

01:21:14.740 --> 01:21:15.570
Hey!

01:21:23.790 --> 01:21:28.210
Please. I don't care if
I lose everything precious to me.

01:21:28.670 --> 01:21:32.130
So right now,
please work a miracle for everyone.

01:21:34.590 --> 01:21:35.720
<i>That's right...</i>

01:21:37.140 --> 01:21:39.520
<i>Back there, I made a wish...</i>

01:21:40.720 --> 01:21:43.980
<i>I wanted a miracle,</i>
<i>even if what I held precious was lost.</i>

01:21:45.690 --> 01:21:46.650
<i>And so...</i>

01:21:47.860 --> 01:21:49.440
<i>I was born.</i>

01:22:10.500 --> 01:22:12.090
What is that song?

01:22:13.220 --> 01:22:17.850
No... That song will
take my magic array and...!

01:22:18.800 --> 01:22:19.930
Stop!

01:22:20.930 --> 01:22:24.390
If you extend that kind of power now...

01:22:25.480 --> 01:22:28.060
they'll fall apart... My hopes...

01:22:29.310 --> 01:22:30.730
My dreams...!

01:23:08.020 --> 01:23:09.980
Master, what do we do?

01:23:10.310 --> 01:23:11.480
It's coming down!

01:23:15.900 --> 01:23:19.950
"Wow! We're flying through
the air," says Misaka Misaka...

01:23:20.070 --> 01:23:23.410
Tch, this is the only time
I'm doing this, understand?!

01:23:36.630 --> 01:23:37.470
Captain...

01:23:40.260 --> 01:23:41.090
Endymion is...

01:23:41.970 --> 01:23:44.970
Endymion is moving away
from its descent course.

01:23:45.270 --> 01:23:47.560
It's going to avoid
a collision with the earth!

01:24:03.280 --> 01:24:04.200
You did it.

01:24:05.740 --> 01:24:07.500
I'm sure the world must have heard...

01:24:08.750 --> 01:24:09.960
your song.

01:24:28.270 --> 01:24:33.650
I wonder, what did
that young woman end up being?

01:24:33.770 --> 01:24:34.610
<i>Yes, indeed.</i>

01:24:35.690 --> 01:24:38.900
<i>If I had to say,</i>
<i>she might have been a wish.</i>

01:24:39.400 --> 01:24:40.450
A wish?

01:24:41.280 --> 01:24:43.370
Even if it is not the work of an esper,

01:24:43.700 --> 01:24:47.160
a person's wishes can distort
their subjectivity.

01:24:48.290 --> 01:24:52.210
If multiple wishes are
all given the same direction,

01:24:52.790 --> 01:24:56.250
their power can
even interfere with causality.

01:24:57.420 --> 01:25:00.470
That power could divide a young girl,

01:25:00.720 --> 01:25:03.260
and alter the fate of many people.

01:25:03.340 --> 01:25:08.600
And then, the distortion caused
by the two becoming one again

01:25:08.810 --> 01:25:10.980
has worked its own miracle.

01:25:12.270 --> 01:25:15.650
Ladylee has performed quite
the fascinating experiment.

01:25:16.480 --> 01:25:20.320
All in all, it is unfortunate
that she cannot die.

01:25:22.570 --> 01:25:23.410
Say, Toma,

01:25:24.110 --> 01:25:25.660
was Arisa really...?

01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:27.200
No.

01:25:27.490 --> 01:25:31.620
I mean, I actually touched her,
with my right hand.

01:25:32.870 --> 01:25:35.500
So she was not just some illusion.

01:25:36.630 --> 01:25:37.460
She liked songs

01:25:38.300 --> 01:25:40.420
and delighting others with songs,

01:25:40.960 --> 01:25:43.430
and was otherwise just a normal girl.

01:25:44.010 --> 01:25:45.930
Mm-hmm, you're right.

01:26:02.530 --> 01:26:04.280
Toma, did you hear that, too?

01:26:05.200 --> 01:26:06.030
Yeah!
